      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_bf665d5800a7ec607be8461ddfd6fef90e878676c82e3a72da143f41b887a30b",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Source fact: exp((sin z)^2) has double-exponential decay in the imaginary direction in a narrow real strip. The source multiplies F by scaled versions of this kernel and applies maximum modulus on two rectangles; the second weighted function also contains X^(s-s_2), chosen to balance the vertical sides, and propagates an upper bound to the left target point. Interpretation: the kernel suppresses weakly controlled remote horizontal edges while X redistributes the remaining vertical costs. Boundary: this is upper-bound propagation, not the final contradiction, and it depends on Step I Ingham lines, separate vertical bounds, and sufficiently large constants. Uncertainty: a variable in Lemma 5.3 and most scalings and exponents are OCR-corrupted.",
